factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 8 problems
  reel_script says the tree fell 'on the old national highway' (பழைய தேசிய நெடுஞ்சாலை) without the article's specification that it fell on the Karur national highway near Chellandiyamman temple; the article itself is inconsistent, but the draft's 'பழைய' framing is mixed with 'Karur highway' context in the article.
  reel_script says 'பெரிய விபத்து தவிர்க்கப்பட்டது' – article says only 'விபத்து தவிா்க்கப்பட்டது'; the adjective 'பெரிய' is an invented detail.
  reel_script says the protesters 'போராட்டத்தில் ஈடுபட முயன்றனர்' – article says they tried to start a road blockade (சாலை மறியல்), and that they dispersed after officials' assurance; the draft omits that they dispersed and mischaracterizes the action as a general protest.
  reel_script omits that the residents' water-logging was cleared with a JCB/pokleyn vehicle while the draft's slide mentions it, fine, but the reel_script states 'அதிகாரிகள் நடவடிக்கை எடுக்கப்படும் என உறுதியளித்தனர்' without naming the police officers (துணைக் கண்காணிப்பாளர் and inspector) – acceptable wording, not a problem.
  reel_script and slides_spec attribute the Mohanur road old tamarind tree fall ('மோகனூர் சாலையில் பழைய புளியமரமும் சாய்ந்தது') correctly, but the caption and slide present the 'Jedarpalayam' knee-deep water as on the 'சாலையில' generally, which matches the article; no issue there.
  slides_spec hl1 'பரமத்தி வேலூரில் பெரிய மரம் சாய்ந்தது' and slide 'என்ன நடந்தது?' claim 'சாலையின் நடுவே விழுந்தது' – the article says the tree fell onto the road (சாலையில் சாய்ந்தது) and later 'சாலையின் நடுவே', so this is supported; no issue.
  caption states 'பழைய தேசிய நெடுஞ்சாலையில்' while the article's main sentence says 'பழைய தேசிய நெடுஞ்சாலையில்' in one place and 'கரூா் தேசிய நெடுஞ்சாலையில்' in another – the draft picks the first without noting the Karur highway, which is a mixed-fact issue within the same story as the article itself.
  reel_script omits the main story's cause detail of the heavy rain being 'சனிக்கிழமை இரவு பெய்த கனமழை' – this is present; however reel_script omits the fact that the tree-cutting team came from Pugalur fire station (Karur district), an important actor of the article, which is missing from the script.
